1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,132
To recap.

2
00:00:01,132 --> 00:00:10,367
One: an eigenvector is a direction that a matrix only stretches or flips, written A v equals lambda v.

3
00:00:10,367 --> 00:00:17,411
Two: we find the eigenvalues by solving the determinant of A minus lambda I equals zero.

4
00:00:17,411 --> 00:00:22,897
Three: each eigenvalue is the scaling factor along its eigenvector.

5
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:24,191
Thanks for watching.

6
00:00:24,191 --> 00:00:29,264
References, music credit and AI disclosure are on screen.

